            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0522" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg440"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>The Marquis Montholon to Mr. Hunter</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of France to the United
                                States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-08-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 4, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I hasten to let you know that I have just
                    received from his excellency Marshal Bazaine a despatch announcing to me that
                    the government of Mexico has decided that the American materiel unduly taken
                    over to the Mexican bank on the surrender of Brownsville, to which the letter of
                    your excellency addressed to me the 12th July relates, should be restored
                    without delay to the federal authorities, and that orders were immediately sent
                    to Matamoras to assure the execution of this decision.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the assurances of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MONTHOLON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Hunter</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
